[{:seon.task/name "a-resource-name-stays-in-its-root"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by jolt/similar-finds-helpers-by-embedding (2026-10-23): in a worktree nested under the main tree (next/.worktrees/NAME), `seon.config-test/an-unknown-key-refuses-boot-naming-it` and `an-invalid-value-refuses-boot-naming-each-key` read the MAIN tree's resources/seon/config/default.edn, so a branch that adds config keys is red there and one that removes keys could be falsely green. Cause: Jolt's resource lookup over jolt.loader's roots, `resource-candidate` (reference-code/jolt/host/chez/java/io.ss, called from `resolve-resource`) builds root + \"/\" + name with no check that the normalized path stays under root, and aero's adaptive resolver tries ``clojure.java.io/resource`` before the including file's directory, so test/seon/config/unknown-key.edn's #include \"../../../resources/seon/config/default.edn\" climbs from the worktree's src/ root out to next/resources/. The JVM's resource lookup answers nil for a name that leaves its root. Reproduction, in a nested worktree: HOME=$PWD/target/home JOLT_PWD=$PWD target/jolt/jolt -A:test -e '(println (str (clojure.java.io/resource \"../../../resources/seon/config/default.edn\")))' prints a file: URL into the main tree; the JVM prints nil. Correct, in our Jolt fork on a jolt/<topic> branch: `resource-candidate` answers no candidate for a name whose normalized path leaves its root. Notes: side-session-notes config-include-leak.md."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{jolt.loader-test/clojure-java-io-resource-resources-seon-config-default}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-cache-bound-is-tested-at-the-targets-size-before-release"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: Deep fixes. What exists: Jolt keeps its compiled-code cache under a byte budget, least recently used first (``JOLT_CACHE_MB``, Jolt `b12a223d`; docs/source.md#shared-build-caches), and bin/env sets it to 32768 so that nothing is evicted while we develop (owner, 2026-11-11: \"Is this going to slow down development? Will we be able to lower this later to test before we release it?\"). Measured 2026-11-11 on the shared cache: one worktree's builds and tests on a new runtime, 354 MB in 890 artifacts; every session's worktrees on one runtime over a day and a half, 3.2 GB in 3,336; the whole cache 4.6 GB in four generations. So 4096 holds one checkout's working set about ten times over and is the candidate for the 16 GB target. Correct, before a release: the bound is set from the working set of one checkout's full build and prove measured on a clean cache, and a run at that bound shows no artifact of the running tree evicted (no recompile of a namespace the same process tree compiled) and the cache directory at or under the bound after it. Proof when built: a check step that builds and proves one tree with ``JOLT_CACHE_MB`` at the release number on an empty cache directory of its own, and counts recompiles of already-compiled namespaces (0) and the directory's bytes (at most the bound)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}
]
